# Competition Brief - Summary

**Competition:** Axis MOVES 2026 - "Organization of the Future: Design for 2035"
**Host:** Axis Bank, run via [InsideKampus](https://insidekampus.com/competition/axis-moves-2026)
**Format:** Team challenge (2 students per team, same campus), multi-round - team
registration, a simulation assessment, a short PPT round, a detailed PPT round, and a
Grand Finale in Mumbai.

The full official brief document is intentionally **not re-hosted** in this repository,
since it's the organizer's copyrighted material rather than our own work - see the
competition page linked above for the original.

## What the brief asked teams to do

Act as Axis Bank's Transformation Council and design the bank for 2035: identify **one**
enterprise-level transformational change - a new business model, operating model,
workforce model, customer model, AI ecosystem, distribution model, or organizational
capability - and show how it would work in practice (roles, processes, governance,
technology enablement, adoption pathway) with a quantified business impact case.

Teams were explicitly told **not** to submit:
- AI chatbot ideas
- Incremental process automation
- Product feature improvements
- Technology-only solutions without an operating-model change
- Solutions lacking measurable business impact

## Judging criteria (equally weighted, 20% each)

| Criterion | Weight |
|---|---|
| Boldness of Vision | 20% |
| Strategic Relevance | 20% |
| Demonstrable Business Impact | 20% |
| Operating Model & Execution Feasibility | 20% |
| Storytelling & Communication | 20% |

